# The repo-root .gitignore matches studies/*/*/<x> (two levels). The contrasts in
# this folder sit one level deeper (studies/fungi/yeast_convergence/<id>/), so the
# same class-1 (ephemeral, regenerable) rules are repeated here for them.
# Same reasons as the root file: never commit fetched data, materialized inputs,
# annotation extracts, enrichment caches or pipeline results.
*/data/
*/data_dir
*/data_dir_*
*/annotations/
*/annotations_orig/
*/results/
*/analysis/enrichment/outputs/cache/
*/analysis/pfam_hmmsearch/
# Cross-contrast comparison working files (the summary tables are tracked).
analysis/convergence/tmp/
# BUSCO per-proteome run directories (regenerable with bin/run_busco_proteomes.sh)
analysis/busco/runs/
analysis/convergence/term_recurrence.tsv
# Taxonomy screens (bin/lichen_taxcheck.sh, bin/candidate_taxcheck.sh): the hit tables and query lists are
# not tracked (their SHA-256 is in each PROVENANCE.yaml); summary.tsv and the provenance are.
analysis/lichen_check/hits.tsv.zst
analysis/lichen_check/queries.txt
analysis/lichen_check/diamond.log
analysis/lichen_check/best_hits.tsv.gz
*/analysis/candidate_taxcheck/hits.tsv.zst
*/analysis/candidate_taxcheck/queries.txt
*/analysis/candidate_taxcheck/diamond.log
# Growth-form literature work (bin/gf_lit.py): source article XML, full sentence text and scratch
# runs are regenerable and must not be committed (CLAUDE.md data class 1). The tables, the gold sets,
# the prompts and their provenance are tracked.
growth_form/cache/
growth_form/sentences/
growth_form/logs/
growth_form/gold_cache/
growth_form/stage_d_input/
growth_form_v*_scratch/
